WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
7.3 million Israelis vote in an election that could end Netanyahu's rule after three years of war. This is Omni View, episode 218. Himalayan border face-offs, charges around a British air base, and an execution in Iran come after the vote. Then how a party-less system actually produces a government. Poles opened across Israel on Tuesday morning for a vote that will decide the makeup of the 120-seat kineset, the country's parliament. Exit polls are expected shortly after

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.580
voting ends at 10 p.m. local time, though a final result may take days or weeks. 1.2 million

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:42.100
Palestinian citizens of Israel are eligible to take part, and diplomats already cast ballots

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.840
at Israeli missions abroad on October 20th. The contest follows conflict that began with the

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:54.160
October 7th 2023 attacks. It carries disputes over alleged failures that allowed those attacks,

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:00.560
The handling of captives taken to Gaza, alleged corruption and ultra-orthodox military service.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.280
Al Jazeera presents the ballot as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.900
through the Gaza War and tensions with Iran.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:15.080
That account also notes a United Nations or UN panel has accused Israel of extermination

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.580
in the West Bank and genocide in Gaza.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.180
Final polls published Friday in that telling showed Netanyahu's coalition neck-and-neck

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:28.520
with the opposition, or trailing it slightly, so the referendum frame does not claim a route.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:34.320
The Guardian's coverage runs on coalition math. Recent polls show that coalition trailing

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.920
or tied with an opposition block led by former military chief Gadi Eisenkott.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:44.540
The strongest case for reading the night as an arithmetic fight in that reporting is that neither

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:50.460
camp governs unless it can secure 61 seats needed for a majority. The first figures will appear

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:55.080
on news channels and the Central Elections Committee website, and a clear majority could

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.640
still require extended coalition negotiations.

00:01:58.797 --> 00:02:04.317
Shatrajit Kapoor, Director-General of India's Indo-Tibetan Border Police, the force that

00:02:04.317 --> 00:02:09.417
patrols the Himalayan Frontier, stated that confrontations with Chinese troops were continuing

00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:10.617
at multiple locations.

00:02:11.337 --> 00:02:15.777
Face-offs happened at several locations in Arunachal Pradesh in the past few days.

00:02:15.777 --> 00:02:20.817
India and Chinese troops have engaged in new confrontations at multiple points along

00:02:20.817 --> 00:02:21.417
that border.

00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:26.217
The incidents come during a fragile period of diplomatic thought between the two countries.

00:02:26.797 --> 00:02:31.517
The South China Morning Post reports the renewed tensions as a direct test of recent efforts

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:37.017
to stabilize relations, and notes that Indian officials describe the confrontations as ongoing

00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:38.237
rather than resolved.

00:02:38.877 --> 00:02:43.617
In that framing, the face-offs are evidence that the reproachment remains vulnerable to border

00:02:43.617 --> 00:02:49.278
incidents that have previously led to prolonged standoffs. British prosecutors have charged

00:02:49.278 --> 00:02:55.358
Mohamed Abdul Kareem, age 24, with assisting a foreign intelligence service, and new man

00:02:55.358 --> 00:03:00.858
Eskir, age 24, with entering a prohibited place for a purpose-prejudicial to the United

00:03:00.858 --> 00:03:06.878
Kingdom, or UK. The BBC reports that the charges stem from an incident near the Gloucestershire

00:03:06.878 --> 00:03:12.658
airbase on September 27th, when three suspicious vehicles were stopped and several men arrested,

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:18.678
And that a 25-year-old UK Iranian national was re-arrested last week, but released without

00:03:18.678 --> 00:03:20.678
charge while remaining on police bail.

00:03:21.658 --> 00:03:25.618
Counterterrorism police have described Iranian state involvement as highly likely.

00:03:26.278 --> 00:03:30.658
Eight men in total have been arrested as part of the investigation, with six remaining

00:03:30.658 --> 00:03:31.578
on police bail.

00:03:32.338 --> 00:03:36.618
Deutsche Walla states that the base has been used by U.S. forces for strikes on Iran.

00:03:36.618 --> 00:03:41.938
that U.S. bombers were withdrawn from Fairford on security grounds shortly after the arrests,

00:03:42.518 --> 00:03:47.318
and that two suspects were re-arrested on October 20th on suspicion of assisting a foreign

00:03:47.318 --> 00:03:52.438
intelligence service. The men will appear at Westminster magistrate's court later on Tuesday.

00:03:53.687 --> 00:03:58.287
Alicina Mustafavi, a mountaineer who had climbed several of the world's highest peaks including

00:03:58.287 --> 00:04:04.127
Mount Everest, was executed on October 14th after being arrested during earlier anti-government

00:04:04.127 --> 00:04:09.747
protests. Two other athletes have been executed in recent months, and at least six more face

00:04:09.747 --> 00:04:15.987
the same risk, according to activist groups. Siavash Jamshidi Hirabadi, a Taekwondo athlete,

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:21.927
was killed at the start of October. Mixed martial arts fighter Golem Reza Kani Shekarab was

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:27.007
hanged in May. The Guardian reports the killings as part of a broader pattern targeting sports

00:04:27.007 --> 00:04:32.387
figures arrested in connection with protests, and says fears are growing for more Iranian athletes

00:04:32.387 --> 00:04:39.964
facing execution. South Korea's economy, Asia's fourth largest expanded 3.4% year-on-year in the

00:04:39.964 --> 00:04:46.284
latest quarter, exceeding forecasts. Strong demand for semiconductors linked to artificial intelligence

00:04:46.284 --> 00:04:52.484
or AI supported the growth. Al Jazeera attributes the outperformance to the semiconductor sector's

00:04:52.484 --> 00:04:59.568
role in global AI supply chains and notes that the figure-beat market expectations. UK businesses

00:04:59.568 --> 00:05:04.268
in significant financial distress reached their highest recorded level in the third quarter,

00:05:04.748 --> 00:05:12.088
according to an administrator's report. The report counted 738,144 firms in that condition.

00:05:12.588 --> 00:05:19.268
The highest since the measure began in 2004. The figure rose 1.6% from the same period last year.

00:05:19.948 --> 00:05:24.008
The Guardian links the increase to pressure on the chancellor to provide additional private

00:05:24.008 --> 00:05:29.468
sector support in the upcoming budget. Calls are growing in that reporting for more help for

00:05:29.468 --> 00:05:33.348
businesses facing rising costs of essentials including food and fuel.

00:05:34.421 --> 00:05:39.301
Morocco overtaking South Africa as Africa's fourth most attractive investment destination

00:05:39.301 --> 00:05:44.261
is progress worth knowing, after years of industrialization and faster growth.

00:05:44.741 --> 00:05:49.801
The shift appeared in Rand Merchant Banks' Continental Investment Ranking, a bank survey

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:55.061
of where capital is most likely to go, and reflects a sustained policy focus on manufacturing

00:05:55.061 --> 00:05:56.081
and infrastructure.

00:05:56.081 --> 00:06:02.061
Blumberg reports the ranking change as evidence of diverging economic trajectories on the continent,

00:06:02.421 --> 00:06:07.601
while noting that South Africa remains the largest economy by overall size. That account

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:12.581
attributes Morocco's rise to consistent industrial policies that have attracted foreign capital

00:06:12.581 --> 00:06:19.325
in sectors beyond raw materials. Elsewhere, Kylian and Bape lost two major Chinese sponsors after

00:06:19.325 --> 00:06:25.505
a video showed the footballer joking about a meme of Mao Zedong as a Chinese dictator. A cruise ship

00:06:25.505 --> 00:06:29.825
crashed into two container ships during a storm, and German police are investigating

00:06:29.825 --> 00:06:34.525
the captain after the vessel collided with docked ships and strong winds, cancelling

00:06:34.525 --> 00:06:35.425
a planned voyage.

00:06:36.105 --> 00:06:40.905
Pop Mart's third quarter-sales fell by up to 50% from a year earlier as the Laboubou

00:06:40.905 --> 00:06:43.865
Fad cooled and demand for its popular characters faded.

00:06:44.817 --> 00:06:49.237
To really understand how a party-list vote becomes a government, you have to look past

00:06:49.237 --> 00:06:53.217
the night's projection and into the bargaining that starts once the count is certified.

00:06:53.217 --> 00:06:57.617
The common misunderstanding is that the seat tally itself decides who won.

00:06:58.197 --> 00:07:01.437
The system allocates seats strictly by party list vote share.

00:07:01.997 --> 00:07:06.357
You vote for a party slate, not a local candidate, and seats follow that share.

00:07:07.017 --> 00:07:11.977
A low threshold means even small parties can enter the kineset and hold leverage in coalition

00:07:11.977 --> 00:07:12.397
talks.

00:07:13.037 --> 00:07:17.797
The structure rewards parties that can deliver narrow but reliable blocks of seats to larger

00:07:17.797 --> 00:07:18.317
alliances.

00:07:18.317 --> 00:07:23.437
Historical patterns show that prime ministers have repeatedly traded policy concessions

00:07:23.437 --> 00:07:27.437
on settlements, religious issues, or budgets to secure those seats.

00:07:28.057 --> 00:07:32.937
The same low threshold rule has produced multi-party coalitions in every recent caness it.

00:07:33.397 --> 00:07:38.517
That makes the post-election negotiation phase the true test of any reported lead, not

00:07:38.517 --> 00:07:40.157
the first projection on television.

00:07:40.797 --> 00:07:45.737
When a block is declared the winner on exit polls, those numbers may not guarantee a stable

00:07:45.737 --> 00:07:46.237
majority.

00:07:46.237 --> 00:07:48.717
community. They may only open extended bargaining.

00:07:49.397 --> 00:07:53.597
Primary documents from the Central Elections Committee provide the raw seat totals that

00:07:53.597 --> 00:07:58.297
determine who actually controls the majority threshold. Compare those official figures

00:07:58.297 --> 00:08:04.617
against the initial exit poll averages published by channels 11, 12, and 13, and you can see

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:09.337
how much the final count shifts while the ballots are still being added up. Al Jazeera

00:08:09.337 --> 00:08:14.197
frames the vote around domestic accountability for war leadership, captives, and corruption.

00:08:14.197 --> 00:08:19.637
While the Guardian frames it as coalition arithmetic, who can actually assemble a government?

00:08:20.197 --> 00:08:25.177
After the official Israeli seat tally is certified, smaller parties that cross the threshold

00:08:25.177 --> 00:08:29.417
will publish the coalition demands that decide whether anyone can assemble a majority.

00:08:30.077 --> 00:08:31.817
That wraps up today's omniview.

